# Spacing and yield [DRAFT]

Spacing is the decision that is hardest to undo: wide rows give each tree
room to fill out, narrow rows raise yield per square metre for the first
several years and then give it back as the canopy closes.

:::{draft}
Internal note, remove before publishing: this whole section still needs a
second pass once this year's harvest count is in.
:::

At four metres a garden fits very few trees; at two metres the canopy
closes by year six and yield per tree falls even as yield per square
metre holds up for a while.

